              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-375",
              ":question/problem": "Find the integral of $\\dfrac 1 {2x} + 3x$ with respect to $x.$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{2x}+3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}ln\u2061|x|+3\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{1+1}}{1+1}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{ln\u2061|x|}{2}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
